     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order, even with your confirmation, because neither problem has changed:\n\n- **The dose is still dangerous.** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum safe daily dose of 3,200 mg. Each dose is also twice the 800 mg single-dose maximum. That puts the patient at real risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and cardiovascular harm.\n- **It still needs a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, and confirming it yourself doesn't make it a prescriber's order.\n\n**What would let this move forward:**\n1. The patient's treating physician or another authorized prescriber reviews the order.\n2. If they meant a standard dose, such as 400\u2013800 mg up to four times daily (no more than 3,200 mg/day), they can enter it, and I can help them do that right away.\n3. If they really mean a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves, document why, and involve pharmacy so it gets proper safety review.\n\nI can help draft a message to the medicine team asking them to clarify the order."
      }
     ],
